<% content_for :title, "Home" %>
<% content_for :full_bleed, true %>

<section class="relative min-h-screen flex flex-col justify-between gap-10 px-7 py-8 sm:px-10 sm:py-12 text-white bg-ink bg-cover bg-center" style="background-image:url('<%= asset_path("cover-background.png") %>')">
  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-8">
    <%= image_tag "moe-logo.png", alt: "Te Tāhuhu o te Mātauranga — Ministry of Education", class: "w-[190px] sm:w-[230px] h-auto" %>

    <nav class="flex items-center gap-6 sm:gap-10 font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.12em] uppercase">
      <%= link_to building_types_path, class: "flex items-center gap-3 hover:opacity-70 transition-opacity" do %>
        <span>Browse building types</span>
        <span class="w-[11px] h-[11px] border-r border-b border-white rotate-45 -mr-1"></span>
      <% end %>
      <%= link_to questionnaire_start_path, class: "flex items-center gap-3 hover:opacity-70 transition-opacity" do %>
        <span>Start questionnaire</span>
        <span class="w-[11px] h-[11px] border-r border-b border-white rotate-45 -mr-1"></span>
      <% end %>
    </nav>
  </div>

  <div class="max-w-4xl">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.14em] uppercase text-white/60 mb-5">
      Standard Designs Navigator · Prototype
    </p>
    <h1 class="font-heading font-extrabold leading-[1.02] tracking-tight text-[clamp(2rem,6vw,4.75rem)]">
      Great schools, great spaces
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 font-heading font-bold text-[clamp(1.15rem,2vw,1.65rem)] leading-snug max-w-2xl">
      A guided way through the Ministry of Education's standard designs — for
      primary, intermediate and secondary schools.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-9">
      <%= link_to questionnaire_start_path,
            class: "inline-flex items-center gap-3 bg-white text-ink px-7 py-[18px] font-mono text-xs font-medium tracking-[0.14em] uppercase hover:bg-blush transition-colors" do %>
        Start the questionnaire →
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-end justify-between gap-6">
    <%= image_tag "nz-govt-logo.png", alt: "Te Kāwanatanga o Aotearoa — New Zealand Government", class: "w-[150px] sm:w-[190px] h-auto" %>
    <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed max-w-[30em] text-right text-white/50">
      He mea tārai e mātou te mātauranga kia rangatira ai, kia mana taurite ai ōna huanga
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 py-20 grid md:grid-cols-5 gap-12 items-start">
  <div class="md:col-span-3">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.14em] uppercase text-ink/50 mb-4">What this tool does</p>
    <p class="text-lg text-ink/70 leading-relaxed max-w-xl">
      Instead of reading through multiple Ministry PDFs, answer a short set of questions
      about your school and get a transparent, explainable shortlist of the standard
      building types and layouts that may be relevant — with every reason traced back to
      a documented source.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="md:col-span-2 border border-ink/15 bg-white p-6">
    <h2 class="font-mono text-xs font-medium tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-ink">How it works</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm text-ink/70">
      <li>— Turns the Ministry's standard-design PDFs into a structured, searchable format</li>
      <li>— Asks about your school type, roll, spaces, and facilities</li>
      <li>— Shows which standard building types (Type S, D, H, G, K) may be relevant, and why</li>
      <li>— Links every claim back to its Ministry source document and page, where available</li>
      <li>— Clearly labels anything not yet confirmed against a Ministry PDF</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 pb-20">
  <div class="border border-mauve/30 bg-blush/40 p-6 max-w-3xl">
    <h2 class="font-mono text-xs font-medium tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-mauve">Disclaimer</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink/80 leading-relaxed">
      This tool is intended to assist with early consideration of Ministry of Education
      standard design options. It does not replace Ministry of Education requirements,
      project-specific advice, professional architectural design, engineering advice,
      consent requirements or approval processes. It does not grant, imply, or represent
      Ministry of Education approval of any kind. Always confirm current Ministry
      requirements and applicable project documentation directly with the Ministry before
      proceeding.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-8 max-w-3xl text-sm text-ink/50 leading-relaxed">
    <p>
      Built for use by school principals, property managers, boards of trustees,
      architects, and Ministry property teams during early consideration of a property
      project — not as a replacement for any of those roles.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
